.TH tkufiledialog n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkufiledialog
.PP
Modal \fBopen / save / directory\fR chooser on top of \fBtkupath\fR + \fBtkufilelist\fR. Same look as the explorer stack; local \fBtuprovider\fR by default, optional \fB\-provider\fR for ZIP/remote. Returns a path (or a list with \fB\-multiple\fR), or \fB""\fR / \fB{}\fR if cancelled. Tk 8.6+ and 9.x.
.PP
Not a full file manager — a compact dialog for “pick this file/folder”.
.SS API
.CS
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::open      ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::save      ?options?
::tkutils::tkufiledialog::directory ?options?
.CE
.SS Options
.TS
l l.
Option	Meaning
\fB\-parent w\fR	toplevel for transient / placement
\fB\-title t\fR	window title
\fB\-initialdir d\fR	start directory (default: \fB$HOME\fR or \fBpwd\fR)
\fB\-provider p\fR	\fBtuprovider\fR (default: fresh local)
\fB\-filetypes {{Label {.ext}}…}\fR	type combobox → list filter (first ext used)
\fB\-multiple 0|1\fR	open only: return a list of paths
\fB\-showhidden 0|1\fR	show dotfiles
\fB\-initialfile name\fR	save only: prefill name entry
\fB\-defaultextension .ext\fR	save only: append if name has no extension
.TE
.SS Behaviour
.IP \(bu
Double\-click a \fBdirectory\fR → navigate; double\-click a \fBfile\fR → OK (open/save).
.IP \(bu
Escape / Cancel → empty result; OK / Return in the name field → confirm.
.IP \(bu
Directory mode lists folders only; OK returns the selected folder or the current path.
.SS Use
.CS
package require tkutils::tkufiledialog

set f [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::open -parent . \
    -title "Open text" -initialdir [pwd] \
    -filetypes {{Text {.txt .md}} {All *}}]

set d [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::directory -parent . -initialdir /tmp]

set s [::tkutils::tkufiledialog::save -parent . \
    -initialfile out.txt -defaultextension .txt]
.CE
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtkufilelist\fR, \fBtkupath\fR, \fBtkudialog\fR, \fBtclutils::tuprovider\fR
